<task id="191" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>A decision whose budget inquiry send failed can be finished from the item: retry sends only the unfinished step, no duplicates, no HTTP 500 (D-222)</title>
    <phase>11 UAT (budget inquiry follow-up, D-222)</phase>
    <gate>startable (after 190 merges, or rebase onto it)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; modifies the decision route's resume logic (.cs) and the DecisionWizard (.tsx).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Ontology-owned data integrity on an append-only route that sends email: a wrong resumability call duplicates an email, a service request or a revision.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>File overlap with task 190 (BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs, DecisionActionExecutors.cs).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ontology</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>A decision whose inquiry send failed after Revise budget landed cannot be finished: the retry replays the failure as HTTP 500 and the Signal is auto-closed. Owner: retryable, and the Signal is not lost meanwhile (D-222 (owner 2026-11-13, notes/decisions.md) (b)).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core, the ontology decision commit route (ledger, resume, step 6) and the Signal evaluator.</role>
  <goal>A Failed send-budget-inquiry step whose service request landed and whose email definitely did not go out is resumable: the retry reuses that service request, sends once, writes the Decision Record once and resolves the Signal; Revise budget is not re-run. A non-resumable replay answers a defined 409, never 500. A system close during the unfinished decision does not strand it.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs:343-347 turns any send exception into SendFailed with the service request id; DecisionActionExecutors.cs:1594-1597 maps it to Failed(write_failed) with Written=[service request]; DecisionCommitService.cs:2049-2074 Failure() makes only a Refused, nothing-written step Resumable. The ledger (LedgerEntry :367, ITenantCache, 7-day OutcomeTtl) stores that; the retry at :654-657 returns it with reasonCode not_resumable and Status Failed, which DecisionCommitEndpoints.cs:74-80 maps to 500. The client already retries a resumable failure (DecisionWizard.tsx:224-239; LockedNote ParameterFields.tsx:59-67). Resume skips Done steps (:1023-1025, :1105-1112) but would run a non-Done inquiry from scratch (second service request). Signal: on failure AfterFailedCommitAsync (DecisionCommitService.cs:1137; DecisionCommitFollowUps.cs:131-134) queues the budget-revision trigger; the evaluator closes ConditionCleared (SignalReevaluationJob.cs ~596-625 -&gt; SignalWriter.CloseAsync :954, log :981). Step 6 already re-closes a system closure since reviewStart (SystemClosedSince :394, pre-check :1279, close :2141); reviewStart is bounded by the 4 h plan-read TTL (Bounded :555).</background>
