  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change this task makes to Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md: no new endpoint, no new DI registration or package unless a criterion names it, and the publish-size delta against a fresh master build is measured and recorded in the task notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every Dataverse write and the email send in this task stay AS THE CALLER (the inquiry email is sent by CommunicationService.SendAsync in SendMode.User, OBO); no app-only fallback is added on any path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Every refusal this task adds or changes on the decision route is a ProblemDetails with a stable reasonCode; never an unhandled 500.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests added in this task cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes. No numeric test target.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">D-222 (owner 2026-11-13, notes/decisions.md) (b): retry re-sends instead of replaying the error; the Signal is not auto-closed while its decision is unfinished. (c): the dev records on MAT-34929-0040 stay as evidence; never edit or delete them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Append-only and D-17 order stand: no compensating delete, record last, the inquiry last, one Decision Record per review id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Only send-budget-inquiry gains resumability, and only when the service request id is known AND the send definitely did not go out (Graph answered an error, or refused before the call). Timeout, cancellation or no answer stays not resumable. Every other step's resumability is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The resumed inquiry reuses the landed service request (from the stored step's Written refs); it never creates a second row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH">One server-side owner per invariant: the unfinished-decision state lives in the route's existing ledger or the Signal row; no plugin, no client-only guard.</constraint>
  </constraints>
