    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Resume of landed steps" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCommitService.cs">:1023-1025 and :1105-1112 carry stored Done steps forward. Extend this; no second journal.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Record-only resume" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCommitService.cs">RecordFailed() :2076-2118 already resumes a no-send record failure (Resumable = !sent). Same shape.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the line references on origin/master; record drift in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="2">BudgetInquiryExecutor: classify a send failure as definitely-not-sent or possibly-sent from what the core throws; carry it on the result and outcome.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a send-only path for a known service request id (InquiryEmailSender.SendAsync, no create), fed on resume from the stored step's Written refs.</step>
    <step order="4">Failure(): a definitely-not-sent inquiry with its service request landed is Resumable; resume runs it send-only; Done steps are skipped as today.</step>
    <step order="5">A replayed non-resumable Failed outcome answers 409 not_resumable with a clear detail (ToHttp), not 500.</step>
    <step order="6">Signal: hold the system close for a Signal whose review holds a resumable failure, OR keep the item reachable and let step 6 re-close it. Record the choice and why in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="7">Client: offer the retry for the new resumable state; word the 409 (decisionDisplay.ts); LockedNote says what the user can do.</step>
    <step order="8">Tests per the acceptance criteria, including the seeding proof.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, the touched test classes and the Signals/Communication unit and data-mutation suites, plus jest on the DecisionWizard folder and tsc/ESLint on touched client files; all pass. Measure the BFF publish-size delta against a fresh master build (§10).</step>
    <step order="10">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status element to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`.</step>
    <step order="11">Record deviations, the publish-size delta and the dev-check result in notes/task-191-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If "resume this one unfinished action with its landed service request" needs a schema change (new Dataverse column or table), STOP and escalate (root CLAUDE.md §6) with options; the ledger entry and DecisionCommitStep.Written are the expected carriers.</trigger>
    <trigger>If CommunicationService does not expose enough to classify a send as definitely-not-sent, STOP and escalate; never treat every send failure as resumable (a re-send could deliver twice).</trigger>
    <trigger>If holding the system close needs evaluator changes beyond the one Signal (episodes, suppression), STOP and escalate first.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>DecisionCommitService.cs:615-760 (ledger, resume), :2049-2118 (resumability); BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs:276-348 (create then send, no send-only entry).</existing>
    <extension>Extend: the resume mechanism and the inquiry executor gain one case each; no new service, endpoint, journal or DI registration.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>On dev the user could not finish the decision: retry gave 500, the Signal closed itself, the revision and service request stand with no record and no email (D-222).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Retry after a failed send">
      <steps>
        <step>On {org}, take Revise budget + Send budget inquiry on a fresh zz- fee/scope Signal with the send made to fail</step>
        <step>Press Record decision again from the item</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Email sent once; one service request, one revision, one Decision Record; Signal resolved with the record linked; no 500 in the network log.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
