  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given Revise budget Done and the inquiry failed definitely-not-sent with service request S landed, a retry of the same review sends the email once with S as the first association, makes no service-request create and does not call the revise-budget executor.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No duplicate service request: exactly one create across both attempts. Seeding proof: break the guard that routes a resumed inquiry send-only, show this test fails, restore, re-run (in task notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No duplicate budget revision: revise-budget runs once across both attempts and its trigger is queued for that one revision.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Decision Record is written exactly once, listing both steps Done with the service request and communication; a further retry returns the Recorded outcome (Replayed) and writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A possibly-sent failure (timeout, cancellation, no answer) is stored not resumable; its retry answers 409 not_resumable naming what landed, and sends or writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every replayed non-resumable Failed outcome answers 409 (not 500) with the stored steps in the extensions; first-attempt status codes are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Signal, order 1 (retry before any system close): resolved and linked as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Signal, order 2 (budget-revision trigger runs between failure and retry): within the plan-read window the retry completes and the Signal ends in this decision's state (Acted, or InquirySent per D-119) with the record linked, never ConditionCleared with no record; outside the window the retry gets a defined refusal (not 500) the item explains.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The unfinished decision is reachable from the item in both orders (server test for the chosen mechanism; reachability rule in task notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Other steps unchanged: a possibly-landed Failed create stays not resumable; a Refused step and a record-only failure resume as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Client: a resumable send failure offers the retry; a 409 not_resumable shows its fixed message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing tests in the touched test classes and folders pass unchanged unless a criterion above names the change; BFF builds with no new warnings in touched files; tsc clean and no new ESLint errors in touched client files.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Dev 2026-11-13 (MAT-34929-0040): revision 03:26:52Z, service request 03:26:54Z, no sprk_communication, Signal closed ConditionCleared 03:27:27Z with no record, retry 500 in 0.6 s; send exception lost to sampling (Graph 502/503/timeouts then). Resume/Retry/Resumable exist; the gap is that a Failed step is never resumable and a replayed failure maps to 500.</notes>
